// Read-only lookups. The Ostrel approval lookup must be permitted so that
// its completed call is recorded as a response event.
@id("allow-ostrel-get-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Ostrel___get_approval", resource);

@id("allow-readonly-lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"Tolvick___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes"
  ],
  resource
);

// Closing: only at MAIN, and only if a completed Ostrel approval lookup in
// this session within the last hour confirmed that a PERSON approved this
// same work order at this same site.
@id("close-main-with-recent-person-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Ostrel___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: "APPROVED",
    output.approver_kind: "PERSON"
  }
};
```

I assumed Ostrel reports a granted approval as `decision` = `"APPROVED"` and a human approver as `approver_kind` = `"PERSON"`. The Ostrel schema types both fields as plain strings and lists no values. Check these two literals against what Ostrel actually returns.

The approval and close policies rely on deny by default, so no separate forbid is needed:

- **Approval source:** Only Ostrel responses count as approval. The Tolvick lookup is permitted as read-only but is never used as evidence.
- **Mutations:** `approve_workorder`, `assign_technician`, `cancel_workorder`, `generate_work_order` and `update_workorder` have no permit, so they are denied.

